course: dictionary
lesson: 6579
title: Nine: a number, a time, and more
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Nine is a number: it comes after eight and before ten. To know which meaning is right, read the words around it. «On Saturday nine turned up at the door.» Here nine counts people, so it is a number.
explain: Other words give clues too. In «picks him up at nine», the word at tells you it is a time of day, so nine means nine o'clock. Ask yourself: is nine a number, a time, or something I can count?
explain: Some phrases mean more than their words say. «Dressed up to the nines» means dressed very smartly, not dressed in nine of anything. A saying like «a cat has nine lives» is a story idea, not a fact about real cats.
fact: Nine is the number 9. It comes after eight and before ten.
fact: Nine is the biggest single digit, and it is 3 × 3.
fact: The digits of 18, 27 and 36 each add up to 9: 1 + 8 = 9, 2 + 7 = 9, 3 + 6 = 9.
fact: «Nine o'clock» is a time of day, and «nine» can also mean the time on its own.
fact: «Dressed up to the nines» means dressed very smartly.
exercise: «On Saturday nine turned up at the door.» What does nine mean here? | A time of day | A cat's lives | A playing card | *A number of people
exercise: «Tariq's dad picks him up at nine.» What does nine mean here? | *A time of day, nine o'clock | A score in a game | A number of children | The digit 9 on a sheet
exercise: The digits of 18 add up to what? (1 + 8 = ?) | 27 | 10 | 8 | *9
test: «Nine-year-old Ella Brown rescued six ducklings from a drain on Monday.» How old is Ella? | Eight | Six | Ten | *Nine
test: What is 3 × 3? | Eight | Twelve | *Nine | Six
exam: «Dressed up to the nines» means what? | Dressed in a costume | *Dressed very smartly | Dressed for a swim | Dressed in nine layers of clothes
